<Application x:Class="RevenantWorkspaceWarden.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:local="clr-namespace:RevenantWorkspaceWarden"
             StartupUri="MainWindow.xaml">
    <Application.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <!-- Revenant house theme, Warden's variant. Same keys, same
                     obsidian and gold ramps as Sidekick; turquoise pulled out of
                     the chrome. Read the header of that file before changing a
                     color — some values are shared with Sidekick and some are
                     deliberately not.

                     ══ WHAT THIS REPLACED, 2026-08-03 ═══════════════════════
                     A local 11-brush palette that lived here. It was navy, not
                     black, despite the naming:

                         BgApp       #080C12   blue channel 10 over red
                         BgSurface   #1C2330   blue channel 20 over red
                         BgStatusBar #1A2D42   blue channel 40 over red

                     Two of its brushes were named for a colour they did not
                     contain — GoldDim was #2A4A62 and BorderGold was #1A2A3A,
                     both navy. Every structural line in the app was drawn by a
                     brush called "BorderGold" that had no gold in it. Its own
                     section comment said "Gunmetal blue accents," so this was
                     known at the time and just never revisited.

                     The theme's obsidian is genuinely neutral (#050506 has one
                     point of blue over red) and BorderGold is #59DFBE81, real
                     gold at 35 percent.

                     Also dropped, both unreferenced anywhere in the app:
                       · GoldDim      — the navy above
                       · GhostFont2   — Ghost Theory 2, retired at Dave's call

                     Every remaining key MainWindow.xaml uses is provided by the
                     theme. Verified by inventorying all 15 StaticResource
                     references before the swap; nothing dangles.        -->
                <ResourceDictionary Source="Theme/RevenantTheme.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Application.Resources>
</Application>
